Default TTS engine: Piper
-------------------------

The default backend and the default Docker image use PiPER from the Open Home
Foundation:

  https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl

The PyPI package `piper-tts` is distributed under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later). It embeds eSpeak-ng
(https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng), which is also GPL-3.0-or-later.

Installing the `piper` extra, or distributing/building the default Docker
image, therefore combines this project with GPL-3.0-or-later components. Such
combined distributions must comply with the GPL (including source availability
for the GPL-covered components). The MIT license continues to apply to this
project's own code.

Piper voice models are downloaded from:

  https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices

Each voice has its own MODEL_CARD with dataset/license information; review it
before redistribution. The default voice `it_IT-paola-medium` is derived from
the dataset referenced in its model card:
https://huggingface.co/datasets/paolapersico1/Voice-Dataset-Italian

Optional backend: pocket-tts
----------------------------

`pocket-tts` (https://github.com/kyutai-labs/pocket-tts) and its voice catalog
(https://huggingface.co/kyutai/tts-voices) have their own licenses, independent
of this project. They are only installed with the `engine` extra and are not
part of the default Docker image.
